With both invariants present, the outer proof now reaches only a Boolean-normalization residual: the path knows the fresh result is false and equal to `noDivisors(C,2)`, but a nested `#if` in the list summary remains unreduced. I’m replacing that conditional expression with two disjoint guarded equations, so the prover can select the exact summary equation from the path condition.
